From 0c81cb02e53ec56162ace459d96f4ff6c1cc812e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shkosugi <sin.kosugi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:16:07 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 36/37] System.Drawing.Common: what comparing every API with
 .NET Framework's found

FrameworkOnCore's parity cases (tests/DrawingParity: every member of .NET Framework's
System.Drawing called on .NET Framework and on the port, the results compared) found these,
each fixed under #if WebFormsForCore or in Core\:

Both:
- Stream.Read may return fewer bytes than asked: icons and animated GIFs read to the end
  (ReadAtLeast), as many bytes as there are.

Windows:
- SystemFonts.DialogFont: the LCID's primary language (ja-JP is 0x0411), as .NET Framework;
  Japanese Windows got Tahoma instead of its UI font.
- Metafile headers: the buffer zeroed before GDI+ fills it (the managed ENHMETAHEADER is larger
  than GDI+'s: EmfPlusHeaderSize and LogicalDpiX/Y were read from memory never written).
- GraphicsPathIterator.Enumerate/CopyData: the arrays' tails zeroed, as .NET Framework.

Linux (libgdiplus, Mono's implementation):
- Graphics.Restore/EndContainer of a state or container not saved by this Graphics: ignored as
  GDI+ does (libgdiplus faulted, SIGSEGV).
- JPEG EXIF: a stream's JPEG under 64 KiB kept its properties (libgdiplus dropped them), and
  values in Motorola order ("MM", most cameras) are given in the machine's, as GDI+ gives them
  (the orientation 6 read as 1536: photos left unturned). Core\Image.ExifByteOrder.cs.
- The resolution of a bitmap made in memory: 96 dpi, as GDI+ (libgdiplus: 0).
- new Bitmap(w, h, stride, format, IntPtr.Zero): the stride is the bitmap's own, as GDI+
  (libgdiplus allocated stride x height bytes: read and written past them).
- Icon for a size: the entry Windows picks (the closest size, then bit depth); it took 32x32
  where Windows takes 16x16. new Icon(stream) leaves the application's stream open.
- Font.FromLogFont/ToLogFont: an application's LOGFONT (its own class, and CharSet.Auto's ANSI
  layout on Unix); the native functions' names (GdipCreateFontFromLogfontW, ...HfontA: not
  found before); the Font is the native one's family, size, style and unit (it was named
  Microsoft Sans Serif, 10); a device context for FromLogFont(lf), which libgdiplus requires.
  Font.FromHfont(IntPtr.Zero) throws as on Windows.
- Graphics.GetNearestColor passes the color in (it answered black).
- A metafile saved (PNG...): drawn, as GDI+ saves it (libgdiplus refused).
- Icon(Type, resource)'s message and Icon.ToString as on Windows; ToolboxBitmapAttribute's
  hash code without images.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
